---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---

<Base title="Our story" description="How Gummikins™ began: handmade crochet companions made one at a time in Wisconsin, for the moments when you can’t be there.">
  <section class="wrap page-head about-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Our story</p>
    <h1>Small creatures.<br />Big comfort.</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap story">
    <figure class="story__photo">
      <img src="/images/placeholder/moss.webp" alt="Three handmade Gummikins sitting together on moss" width="1060" height="494" />
    </figure>
    <div class="story__text prose">
      <p class="story__drop">
        Gummikins started with a ball of yarn, a crochet hook, and someone I loved who lived too far away to hug.
      </p>
      <p>
        I wanted to send something that would sit with them when I couldn’t. Not a card that gets tucked in a drawer, but something soft
        they could pick up, squeeze, and keep close. So I made a little round creature with two shiny eyes and a stitched smile, and
        mailed it off.
      </p>
      <p>
        It went everywhere with them. Then friends asked for one. Then friends of friends. Before long there were Gummikins in college
        dorms, hospital rooms, car cupholders, and on the arm of Grandpa’s TV chair.
      </p>
      <h2>Made by hand, on purpose</h2>
      <p>
        Every Gummikins is still crocheted by hand, one stitch at a time, here in Wisconsin. That means no two are exactly alike. A
        slightly lopsided smile or a rounder tummy isn’t a mistake. It’s how you know a real person made it for you.
      </p>
      <p>
        Leftover yarn never goes to waste. It becomes Little Drops, the tiny Gummikins we tuck into orders as a surprise.
      </p>
      <h2>Comfort, in whatever shape you need</h2>
      <p>
        Some people give Gummikins as gifts. Some keep them close because of how they feel in their hands: the softness, the squish, the
        rhythm of the stitches. Many of our favorite customers are neurodivergent kids, teens, and adults who simply like having something
        soft and quiet to hold. And some people just think they’re wonderful. All of those are good reasons.
      </p>
      <p class="story__sign hand">Thank you for bringing one home. <Icon name="heart" /></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap values">
    <div class="value">
      <h3>Handmade, always</h3>
      <p>Every piece is crocheted, stuffed, and finished by hand. No factories, no shortcuts.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="value">
      <h3>Small batches</h3>
      <p>We make a few at a time, so colors come and go. When they’re gone, they’re gone until the next batch.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="value">
      <h3>Honest about feel</h3>
      <p>We describe exactly how each piece feels, so you can choose what’s right for you or someone you love.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap about-cta">
    <h2>Ready to meet yours?</h2>
    <a class="btn" href="/shop">Shop Gummikins <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-head h1 {
    max-width: 14ch;
  }
  .story {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }
  .story__photo {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .story__photo img {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .story__drop {
    font-family: var(--font-hand);
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.5vw, 2.2rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--chocolate-deep);
  }
  .story__sign {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    color: var(--clay-deep);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .story__sign :global(svg) {
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .story {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr;
      gap: 4.5rem;
      align-items: start;
    }
    .story__photo {
      position: sticky;
      top: 100px;
    }
  }
  .values {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem);
  }
  .value {
    padding: 1.6rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--paper);
  }
  .value:nth-child(1) {
    background: #f6e8c9;
  }
  .value:nth-child(2) {
    background: #e3ecf1;
  }
  .value:nth-child(3) {
    background: #e3e9dc;
  }
  .value p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  @media (min-width: 800px) {
    .values {
      grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr 1fr;
    }
    .value:nth-child(2) {
      translate: 0 1.5rem;
    }
  }
  .about-cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding-top: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 6rem);
  }
</style>
